# NATHAN AI 🚀 — All Interfaces & Build Recovery (additive atlas)

Parent: **NATHAN AI → TABOR ROOT → TABOR 1-2-3 FACTORY → ONE / independent products**.

## What this update actually adds

- A **separate**, searchable recovery and navigation interface at app-factory/nathan-ai/build-recovery/index.html.
- A source-indexed registry.json with **76 existing repository HTML paths** as of the integration branch's starting main snapshot. The recovery interface itself is **new** and therefore not counted among those original 76. All 74 paths are source-file locations, not verified live web deployments.
- An additive list of **92 named system/reference records**, clearly marked recovered references. These do not mean 92 new engines were coded, trained, manufactured or deployed.
- **14 owner-held/historical archive anchors**, identified by filename and description without publishing the owners' private source contents.
- A live read of the existing **73-title Games & Puzzles Atlas** in ../games/catalog.json, preserving its original development stages and without copying or changing that original game catalog.
- Owner-selected source-file session indexing (text preview/search for selected readable files up to 8 MiB, exact download from original File objects). No automatic upload, GitHub publication, IndexedDB or localStorage writes; browser tab navigation/refresh clears chosen files.
- Cross-links from the existing Nathan AI main hub and ONE home, plus a direct listing in the main hub's existing directory.

## Historical recovery vs current source

registry.json includes historical recovery labels from earlier archives: 6,056 master registry rows; 383 selected technical records (273 normalized titles); roughly 5,447 saved file records, which include versions/copies. **These counts are not refreshed repository facts** and are not counts of completed apps, full books, games, or deployable binaries.

The old broader recovery index named Nathan_AI_Recovery_Index_2026-11-01.html is owner-held; the full private archive was not copied into the public code. The offline v073 package and its original modules are likewise **not** asserted present in this GitHub repository; only a source anchor/reference exists here.

Existing Library Mind has a separately published source reader, original book plans and actual language profiles. The separate **33,000,000 address library goal**, **133,333,333 master blueprint goal**, and **66,666 language destination goal** are capacities or ambitions, not delivered counts. The ONE app, Factory, TABOR WORLD, TaborTales, SSS-CS and other distinct products retain independent source and lifecycle rules.

## Original-source boundaries

- Every original user-authored source file remains unchanged by this atlas.
- No prior app code was copied into, rewritten by, or replaced with the recovery atlas.
- Historically named systems without accessible public original source are shown as references or owner-held anchors, not implemented code.
- Exact source quotations belong in owner-controlled originals and may be viewed only through explicit local file selection; analyst-authored labels and descriptions are separate derived metadata.
- Historical/theological/technical assertions remain author-attributed or unverified until sourced.
- No payment, medical-provider connectivity, cloud service, real-time media generation, or app store release is implied.

## Development validation

Run: node --test app-factory/nathan-ai/build-recovery/atlas.test.cjs

All public records are rendered via DOM textContent rather than interpreted as arbitrary HTML. Original locally selected files remain browser-private and are never uploaded. Browser/mobile testing and GitHub Pages rollout are separate from successful repository/CI checks.

**Motto:** Preserve → Index → Relate → Derive; Never Replace. 1+1=2 BUILD. 1-1=0 CLEAR.

## November 2, 2026 — complete public code inventory and safe owner intake

This additive change extends the existing All Interfaces & Build Recovery screen; no original code or JSON registry is replaced.

- **Live public GitHub tree:** the browser requests GitHub's public `main` tree recursively and adds all returned blob paths (including source code, tests, workflow YAML, public JSON, SQL and documents) to the same searchable index. Every file preserves its original GitHub path and reported Git blob ID. GitHub's `truncated` flag is honored. No count is called complete on an API failure.
- **Read public code:** an explicit click opens supported small text/code files within Nathan AI as inert `textContent`; no imported JS, HTML, shell, or Python is ever run. Every file retains its original GitHub source link, including those too large to preview.
- **Integration and patch inventory:** 14 tool/service descriptors, a verified API environment-variable **name-only** registry (no secret values), and ten pull-request references #54–#63. Observed states are dated, not live secrets or automatic sync.
- **Local owner folder selection:** in supporting browsers a user can index an entire selected folder, preserving `webkitRelativePath`, or select files individually. Up to 20,000 selected files per batch are accepted without silent truncation. Sensitive-looking filenames, binaries and large files are never automatically text-previewed. Selected original `File` objects stay in the browser tab.
- **Export manifest:** downloads a metadata-only JSON record of the public registry plus selected local names/paths/sizes. This is **NOT** an original-byte backup or cloud sync. Open the existing Universal Creator Vault and import original ZIP/file archives for persistent *device-local* byte preservation, then export and verify all Vault backup ZIP parts. ONE Connected can link those imported originals to their projects.
- **Security:** No service account tokens, private credentials, wallet seeds, unpublished manuscripts, personal finance records or private source bytes are embedded in public code or transmitted to GitHub by this page. A previously exposed OpenAI API key from earlier archive history still requires independent owner revocation verification.
- **Scope:** public repo files are dynamically indexed, not replicated as a private backend. Private owner-held ZIPs and Drive files cannot be silently scanned or auto-copied by a public GitHub Pages browser. Airtable and other connected ChatGPT services require authorized backend integrations to synchronize actual records. Draft Supabase RLS SQL in open PR #63 remains unapplied.

### Tests and verification

Run `node --test app-factory/nathan-ai/build-recovery/atlas.test.cjs` and `node --check app-factory/nathan-ai/build-recovery/atlas.js`. The preexisting Universal 13 apostrophe syntax issue at `arrowhead-tree-matrix.mjs:15` has an additive parser correction; its tests and the whole Factory CI must pass before a release is called verified. Public GitHub Pages publication and real-device tests remain separately verifiable.

